<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Smart Swimming Pool – Contributing</title><link>https://smart-swimmingpool.com/tags/contributing/</link><description>Recent content in Contributing on Smart Swimming Pool</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-US</language><atom:link href="https://smart-swimmingpool.com/tags/contributing/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Writing Diagrams (Svgbob)</title><link>https://smart-swimmingpool.com/docs/diagrams/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://smart-swimmingpool.com/docs/diagrams/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;Wiring diagrams and other technical drawings are written as plain ASCII art in a
fenced code block with the language &lt;code&gt;svgbob&lt;/code&gt;. At build time the site turns them
into SVG through &lt;a
href="https://kroki.io/"target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Kroki&lt;/a&gt; using
&lt;a
href="https://github.com/ivanceras/svgbob"target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Svgbob&lt;/a&gt;. The diagrams follow the light and
dark theme, and the source stays readable as text on GitHub.&lt;/p&gt;
